# Project stack — this repository

Agent Collections framework repository (vendor-neutral multi-agent core).

## Stack

| Area | Path | Role | Stack |
| ---- | ---- | ---- | ----- |
| Core | `.ai/` | SSOT rules/skills/prompts | Markdown |
| Adapters | `adapters/` | Cursor / Claude / OpenCode packaging | Node `*.mjs` |
| MCP | `mcp/eversis-collections-mcp/` | Skills MCP server | TypeScript |
| Installer | `scripts/` | Consumer install / upgrade | Bash + Node |
| Docs | `docs/architecture/` | Mapping, isolation, AGENTS, selection | Markdown |

## Quality commands

Run from the **repo root** unless noted.

```bash
npm run sync:adapters
npm run sync:adapters:check
npm run mcp:build
npm run mcp:test
bash scripts/setup-agent-collections.test.sh
```

## Conventions

- **Agent entry:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)
- **Framework SSOT:** `.ai/` — adapters and MCP consume it
- **Specs / plans:** `docs/specs/<issue-kebab>/` — `*.research.md`, `*.plan.md`

## Agent skills policy

Presence of a skill package does **not** mean it applies. Before `eversis_skills_get`, read this section and any `docs/context/*.md` notes.

### Always applicable (this framework repo)

| Skill | When |
| ----- | ---- |
| `eversis-fine-handoff` | Fine turn after Implement |
| `eversis-creating-skills`, `eversis-creating-prompts`, `eversis-creating-agents`, `eversis-creating-instructions` | Framework customization work |
| `eversis-orchestrating-implementation` | Implement orchestration |

### Load when task and stack match

| Skill | Load when |
| ----- | --------- |
| `eversis-writing-repo-documentation` | README, CHANGELOG, docs updates |

### Do not load in this repo (unless plan explicitly requires)

| Skill | Reason |
| ----- | ------ |
| `eversis-implementing-filters` | No product list UIs — framework/docs repo only |
| `eversis-implementing-backend`, `eversis-implementing-frontend` | No application backend/frontend in scope |
| `eversis-ba-docs-planner`, `eversis-ba-docs-writer` | Word `.docx` release docs — not this repo's workflow |

**Consumer projects:** replace this section with your product stack.

## Status: Fine — QA comment (mandatory contract)

When **all** planned agent work for an **eversis-implement** thread is finished:

1. Declare **`Fine`** explicitly.
2. **In the same assistant response**, draft the QA comment following the **`eversis-fine-handoff`** skill.
3. Label: **`Draft QA comment — review before posting to Jira`** (or per-story labels when requested).
4. **Never** post to Jira in that turn; publication only after explicit human approval.
